// §A7 (§14.13 + §14.14) — InterruptsOff region + Scheduler.swapContext.
//
// `with InterruptsOff { ... }` opens an interrupt-disabled region.
// The compiler emits a target-specific mask-set on entry and the
// matching restore on every exit path (early return, throw,
// fall-through). The kernel build emits the real instructions
// (DAIF on aarch64, CLI on x86, sstatus on RISC-V); the hosted CI
// build emits a brace block — the discipline is purely static.
//
// Five of the §14.13 rules are statically checked here:
//   1. waitForInterrupt / waitForEvent (rule 5) — deadlock.
//   2. await (rule 2) — resolves through a masked ISR.
//   3. spawn (rule 4) — can't synchronise with the masked region.
//   4. Calls to functions with `using Alloc` or `using Async`
//      (rule 3) — the allocator and async runtime can't run with
//      interrupts masked.
// Nesting is admitted (rule 6); the mask save/restore stacks.
//
// `Scheduler.swapContext(saving, loading)` is the context-switch
// primitive. `Context` is opaque to user code (§14.14 rule 1);
// a kernel allocates a per-task slot in a `@noinit static array`
// and calls `swapContext` to bounce between them. v0.5 accepts
// Context values directly (the spec's MutPtr[Context] / Ptr[Context]
// shape needs `&decl` from §14.6.3 which isn't yet shipped);
// codegen wraps each arg in `&` so the runtime shim sees the
// pointers it expects.

module examples.interrupts_off

// Two task slots. `@noinit` reserves uninitialized .bss storage
// (no constructor runs on Context — its layout is target-
// determined per §14.14 rule 1).
@noinit static slot_a: Context
@noinit static slot_b: Context

// Shared counter the InterruptsOff region mutates atomically.
// The atomic is overkill on a single-hart hosted build but
// matches the kernel pattern.
static counter: Atomic[UInt32] = 0

// Critical-section bump. The runtime executes the body with
// interrupts masked; the hosted shim is a no-op so the body runs
// as a plain brace block.
func critical_bump() {
    with InterruptsOff {
        let v = counter.load(.seqCst)
        counter.store(v + 1, .seqCst)
    }
}

// Nested InterruptsOff regions stack. The inner exit restores to
// the outer's masked state, not to the globally-unmasked state.
func nested_bump() {
    with InterruptsOff {
        let v = counter.load(.seqCst)
        with InterruptsOff {
            counter.store(v + 10, .seqCst)
        }
        counter.store(counter.load(.seqCst) + 1, .seqCst)
    }
}

// Drive Scheduler.swapContext between two Context slots. The
// hosted shim is a no-op; the kernel target replaces it with the
// save/restore sequence.
func switch_tasks() {
    Scheduler.swapContext(slot_a, slot_b)
}
